# NativMix Quality and Release Rules

## Code quality
- Lint with `ruff check lib/` (`--select I --fix` when needed).
- Type-check with `mypy lib/`.
- Prefer Python 3.10+ typing style (`X | None`).
- Never use `except Exception: pass`; log at least `logger.debug`.

## Filesystem and runtime
- Keep XDG compliance: only `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` and `~/.config/nativmix/`.
- Do not use `/tmp/` paths.

## Packaging and releases
- Only the user runs hardware tests and installation (`makepkg` and/or local Flatpak rebuild).
- Never bump versions without explicit user instruction.

### Single release version (no exceptions)
- Source of truth: `lib/nativmix/metadata.py` (`__version__`).
- After an approved bump, **every** file in this repo that embeds a concrete release number must show that same version. “Everywhere” means AUR, OBS, Flatpak, local scripts, CI, Windows packaging, READMEs, changelogs — not only the paths you touched today.
- Do not leave older numbers behind “because that path is unused / legacy”. If a packaging file still carries an older concrete `1.0.x`, the bump is incomplete.
- **`Version: 0` is OBS-only:** Allowed solely as an OBS/`set_version` placeholder in RPM templates (e.g. some fedora/suse specs). The OBS git tag / `_service` revision must still be `v<same as metadata.py>`.
- **Never in local builds:** Local `makepkg`, Flatpak rebuild, `build_local.sh`, Windows packaging, and any manual/CI local package must always build and install the real version from `metadata.py` / `pyproject.toml` — never ship or test as `0`. Local scripts that start from a `Version: 0` template must inject the real version before `rpmbuild` (as fedora/suse `build_local.sh` already do).
- Verification before calling a bump done: search the repo for the **previous** version string; zero hits outside intentional historical changelog entries.

### Bump checklist (update in one change)
- `lib/nativmix/metadata.py`
- `pyproject.toml`
- `packaging/aur/PKGBUILD` + `packaging/aur/.SRCINFO`
- `packaging/aur/PKGBUILD.local` (local makepkg helper — must not lag; prefer reading `pkgver` from `pyproject.toml`)
- `packaging/OSC/nativmix.spec` + `packaging/OSC/_service` + `packaging/OSC/debian.changelog`
- `packaging/fedora/nativmix.spec` / `packaging/suse/nativmix.spec` (`0` only if OBS placeholder; local scripts must inject real version)
- `packaging/debian/changelog` (and related debian packaging if still shipped)
- Root `.SRCINFO` if it exists (must not lag)
- `flatpak/net.knoellix.NativMix.metainfo.xml` release entry when used
- `CHANGELOG.md`, `README.md`, `README_DE.md`

### Other packaging notes
- Keep wiki/README Flatpak notes in sync when packaging docs change.
- Flatpak manifest lives in `flatpak/`; build instructions in `packaging/FLATPAK.md`.
- Escape OBS/RPM macros in comments using `%%`.
- Use `fdupes` as required by packaging flow.
